    "created_at": "2016-05-27T18:43:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-27T18:43:41Z",
    "body": "Suggested revised commit message:\n\n```\nRegression fix: add back origin checks for shared workers\n\nShared workers always needs to perform a same-origin check since if the\nSharedWorkerGlobalScope already exists, no fetching is done, so we\ncannot count on fetching to do the same-origin check. Additionally,\nmodule workers allow cross-origin fetches, but we still want to ensure\na distinct SharedWorkerGlobalScope for cross-origin shared workers.\n\nThis also cleans up “set up a worker environment settings object” with\na more explicit way of referencing the needed environment settings\nobject.\n\nThis regressed through #339 (though that change also had to be made for\nmodule workers).\n\nFixes #1321.\n```\n\nNote especially that the current commit message seems to imply this is only a problem with module workers, but it's more general than that. I'll let you merge instead of changing the commit message drastically myself while doing the merge.\n",
